# tests/rib

## sphere.rib

Written for phase 0's runtime baseline. Not third-party.

## requests/

Minimal, hand-written fixtures, one per RISpec 3.2 request phase 2 added
parse-and-ignore coverage for (`ifelse.rib` covers the four conditional
requests together; `solid.rib` covers `SolidBegin`/`SolidEnd` together --
neither pair is meaningful RIB in isolation). Each is the request under test
followed by a `Sphere`, so a handler that mis-counts its own parameters and
desyncs the token stream is caught by the sphere failing to parse rather than
by the request itself, which a request-in-isolation test would miss.

## corpus/

Real RIB from third-party software, fetched once and checked in so tests are
hermetic (no network at test time).

| File | Source | License | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `menger.rib` | [aqsis/aqsis](https://github.com/aqsis/aqsis) `examples/procedurals/menger/menger.rib`, commit `d258e4ee5200ef29a512f2f4237b06fa3e4bb853` | GPL-2.0 (repo license; this file itself carries no separate header) | The corpus test (`tests/ribdialect_test.cpp`). Shader-free, so it is one of the few Aqsis examples that reaches `RiWorldEnd` without hitting GMAN's missing `plastic`/`matte`-family shader plugins -- see the note below. Exercises `Procedural "DynamicLoad"` and the unbracketed `"fov" 45` parameter form. |
| `bike.rib`, `bikeData.rib.gz` | [aqsis/aqsis](https://github.com/aqsis/aqsis) `examples/features/archives/`, commit `a9ecc18a9ccbddb418b3ad3940c98a541e427461` (model courtesy of jrMan, www.jrman.org, per the file's own header) | GPL-2.0 (repo license) | Exercises `ReadArchive` of a gzip'd file in the same step, over ~5,300 lines of real `Patch`/`Basis`/`TransformBegin` content -- the two hardest step-6/step-7 paths together. Does **not** reach exit 0 end to end: the archive calls `Surface "plastic"`, a shader GMAN has never shipped (only `matte`), so `RiSurfaceV` throws attempting to `dlopen` it. That is a shading-infrastructure gap (Phase 3's territory, `libgman/gmanattributes.cpp` / `gmanloadableshader.cpp`), not a RIB-parsing one -- everything through the point of the `Surface` call parses correctly. Used for the dedicated `ReadArchive`/gzip proof, not the corpus proof. |

Checked in as gzip'd/plain exactly as fetched; `bikeData.rib.gz` is not
decompressed in-tree so the gzip-transparency test has a real gzip'd file to
exercise, not a synthetic one.
